WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 8.3 · Marketing & Communications
Messaging framework

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
A messaging framework helps you and your co-founders describe the work the same way.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:26.281
A messaging framework keeps everyone saying the same essential things in ways that fit each audience. It has a core message, about three supporting messages with proof points, and audience versions.

4
00:00:26.681 --> 00:00:27.281
A message house

5
00:00:27.281 --> 00:00:38.981
Core message: What you do and why it matters, in one or two sentences. For example: A neighbourhood bakery where young people who left school early train in a real kitchen.

6
00:00:38.981 --> 00:00:49.200
Supporting messages: About three reasons to believe or act. For example: Trainees bake real bread; mentors teach real skills; neighbours get good bread at a fair price.

7
00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:59.789
Proof points: Evidence under each message, or what you will measure and when. For example: Four trainees in the pilot; job results measured three months after it ends.

8
00:00:59.789 --> 00:01:09.356
Audience versions: The same core, adapted for each priority audience. For example: Cafés: “Fresh bread each morning, and trainees you could hire.”

9
00:01:09.756 --> 00:01:10.356
Why it matters

10
00:01:10.356 --> 00:01:16.030
1. You and anyone who joins describe the work the same way.

11
00:01:16.030 --> 00:01:20.222
2. Proof points make a new initiative credible.

12
00:01:20.222 --> 00:01:25.785
3. Tested messages make people act, not only understand.

13
00:01:26.185 --> 00:01:26.785
Where you will use it

14
00:01:26.785 --> 00:01:30.607
1. Your website, social posts and newsletters.

15
00:01:30.607 --> 00:01:34.430
2. Your proposals, applications and press kit.

16
00:01:34.430 --> 00:01:39.252
3. Your campaigns and calls to action.

17
00:01:39.652 --> 00:01:40.252
What to avoid

18
00:01:40.252 --> 00:01:44.444
Claiming outcomes you have not seen yet.

19
00:01:44.444 --> 00:01:48.637
Figures you cannot source, or never update.

20
00:01:48.637 --> 00:01:54.200
Printing messages before testing them with real people.

21
00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:56.600
You write your core message, proof points and one audience version.

22
00:01:56.600 --> 00:02:00.600
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

23
00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:05.200
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
